ibly waste bombs or high cards.\n\nMoreover, the landlord has only 1 card — so if my teammate can survive one more round, they might win.\n\nTherefore, best strategy: **pass**, let teammate take the trick and lead.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}  \n\nEvaluation: Although I can beat ♥Q with ♣K, ♣A, or ♦2, the optimal strategy is to let my teammate (who has 3 cards) gain control by winning the trick. The landlord has only 1 card, so we must act quickly to prevent them from winning. However, if I play any card, I take control and force myself to lead — potentially disrupting my teammate’s ability to play their remaining cards. Passing allows my teammate to lead next, giving them a chance to empty their hand.\n\nReason: Maximize cooperation with teammate who is close to winning; avoid seizing control unnecessarily when victory can be achieved through coordination.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
